  "texts": {
    "preamble": "K.Gopalakrishnan vs The Sub Inspector Of Police on 1 January, 2013 Author: A.M.Shaffique Bench: A.M.Shaffique In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable The Chief Justice Mr.Ashok Bhushan & The Honourable Mr.Justice A.M.Shaffique Friday, The 27Th Day Of March 2015/6Th Chaithra, 1937 WP(C).No. 9891 of 2015 (J) --------------------------- Petitioner(S) :- ------------------ K.Gopalakrishnan, Aged 75 Years, S/O.Kumari, Biju Bhavan, Proprietor, Town Bakery, Mallappally P.O. & Village, Pathanamthitta District, Pin - 689 585. By Advs.Sri.N.P.Prajeesh Sri.Bijo Thomas George Respondent(S) :- ------------------ 1. The Sub Inspector Of Police, Keezhvaipur Police Station, Keezhvaipur P.O., Pathanamthitta District, Pin - 689 587. 2. The Inspector Of Police, Mallappally, Pathanamthitta District, Pin - 689 585. 3. The District Police Chief, Pathanamthitta, Pin - 689 645.",
    "facts": "The writ petition is filed by the petitioner seeking police protection inter alia contending that respondents 4 to 6, who were working in his establishment, which is a bakery, for some time has certain dispute in relation to employment. The petitioner does not require to employ them presently and therefore, respondents 4 to 6 are obstructing functioning of the bakery as well as the borma situated in a separate building away from the bakery. According to the petitioner, he is ready and willing to pay compensation to respondents 4 to 6 as fixed by the Labour Court or other competent authority. A conciliation talk held by the District Labour Officer has failed because of the adamant stand taken by respondents 4 to 6. It is submitted that now respondents 4 to 6 are making preparation for obstructing the functioning of the bakery by conducting agitation by blocking the entry to the bakery and also making preparations for attacking the petitioner, his workers, family members etc. 2 :- 2. Learned State Attorney on instructions would submit that on receipt of the complaint from the petitioner, respondents 4 to 6 were called and they were asked not to create any physical obstruction to the functioning of the bakery and they should abide by the orders passed by the labour authorities.",
    "arguments": "",
    "petitioner_arguments": "",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
